        {
          "page": 2,
          "section": "2.2 Alloy production and characterization",
          "quote": "Compact Arc Melter MAM-1 was used to manufacture the alloy. Granules of Cr (99.9 wt%), Mo (99.95 wt%), Ta (99.9 wt%), Ti (99.99 wt%) and V (99.7 wt%) elements were mixed and placed in the arc melter. Before each melting stage, the chamber was vacuumed and flushed with Ar gas at least three times. Produced beads were flipped and remelted at least five times for full mixing and melting of the elements.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "bb38178e92fd1b00:part:001"
