        {
          "page": 3,
          "section": "3.2 Microstructure of Cr10Mo25Ta25Ti15V25 alloys",
          "quote": "Fig. 2b shows that Cr10Mo25Ta25Ti15V25 alloy has a single-phase BCC structure, as opposed to the equilibrium CALPHAD calculations. Since VAM samples are subjected to rapid cooling, sluggish diffusion mechanism does not allow microstructure to show any solid-state phase transformation. Thus, instead of the formation of other BCC and HCP phases, high-temperature phase becomes supersaturated and remains as a single phase at room temperature. The lattice parameter of this phase is measured as 3.18 Å.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "Fig. 2b",
          "chunk_id": "bb38178e92fd1b00:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": 7,
          "section": "3.2",
          "quote": "Li et al. [5 1] ha ve studied the orientation relationship and co - herency of FCC- Ti phase with BCC matrix and found that there is Kur djumo v-Sachs (K–S) orientation relationship between FCC and BCC along {1 1 1} FCC //{1 1 0} BCC with coher ency .",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "bb38178e92fd1b00:part:002"
        }
      ]
    },
