      "attributes": {
        "phase_fraction": null,
        "size": "sub-micron",
        "morphology": "needle-like",
        "location": "nano-crystalline regions",
        "composition": "Ti-rich with some carbon, Ti-C solid solution",
        "identification_status": "experimental"
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 6,
          "section": "3.2 Microstructure",
          "quote": "The diffraction spots encircled by red color belong to BCC RHEA while planes labeled in white color belong to Ti-rich second phase having FCC crystal structure along [110] zone axis. The lattice parameter of this phase has been calculated as 4.42 Å. High annular angular dark field (HAADF) image in Fig. 7b clearly shows the concentration difference in bright and dark grains (and needle-like features) in Fig. 7a. Darker grains have smaller weights compared to the background RHEA composition. EDX analysis also indicated that these regions are rich in titanium with some carbon, which is the solid solution of Ti-C having FCC crystal structure.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "Fig. 7a, 7b",
          "chunk_id": "bb38178e92fd1b00:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": 7,
          "section": "3.2",
          "quote": "Therefore, most of these particles/phases are determined to be FCC Ti-C solid solution phase. It should be not ed that the concentration of the second phase is low enough not to appear in XRD analy ses.",
